message: "If you use this software, please cite the software release, the reproducibility dataset, and the associated manuscript."
title: "Backward Error of the Purcell–Egerváry–Castillo Matrix Inverse"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: Francisco R.
    family-names: Villatoro
    affiliation: Universidad de Málaga
repository-code: "https://github.com/FrancisRVillatoro/backward-error-purcell-egervary-castillo-matrix-inverse"
url: "https://github.com/FrancisRVillatoro/backward-error-purcell-egervary-castillo-matrix-inverse"
abstract: >-
  Frozen software and reproducibility materials for the numerical experiments
  accompanying the manuscript “Backward Error of the Matrix Inverse in the
  Purcell–Egerváry–Castillo Pivoting Transformation”. The release includes
  implementations of the pivoting variants, deterministic campaign generation,
  recovery and population certification, diagonal-dominance audits, defect
  replay, high-precision validation, and canonical post-processing.
keywords:
  - numerical linear algebra
  - matrix inversion
  - backward error
  - floating-point arithmetic
  - pivoting
  - Purcell method
  - Egerváry rank reduction
  - Castillo transformation
  - reproducible research
